## ?? Debug & Troubleshooting

### Check Logs
```bash
# View Android logs
adb logcat

# Filter for app logs
adb logcat | grep meengle

# Save logs
adb logcat > app.log
```
- [ ] No ERROR logs
- [ ] No FATAL logs
- [ ] Check warnings if any

### Chrome DevTools Debugging
```bash
# Open Chrome
chrome://inspect

# Find your app
# Click "inspect"
```
- [ ] Console tab clean (no red errors)
- [ ] Network tab shows successful requests
- [ ] Application tab shows Service Worker
- [ ] Storage shows localStorage/sessionStorage

### Common Issues

#### APK Installation Fails
- [ ] Check: `adb uninstall com.meengle.app`
- [ ] Then: `adb install app-debug.apk`
- [ ] If still fails: Check Android version compatibility
- [ ] Verify APK is valid: `adb shell pm list packages | grep meengle`

#### App Crashes on Launch
- [ ] Check logcat: `adb logcat`
- [ ] Look for NullPointerException or ClassNotFoundException
- [ ] Verify all resources are present
- [ ] Check manifest is valid
- [ ] Try clean rebuild: `cd android && ./gradlew clean`

#### Features Not Working
- [ ] Check API endpoint is correct
- [ ] Verify network connection
- [ ] Check Chrome DevTools console
- [ ] Check network requests succeed
- [ ] Verify API returns expected data

#### Performance Issues
- [ ] Profile with Chrome DevTools
- [ ] Check for memory leaks
- [ ] Optimize images
- [ ] Reduce bundle size if possible
- [ ] Check for infinite loops

#### Offline Mode Not Working
- [ ] Verify service-worker.js is loaded
- [ ] Check IndexedDB in DevTools
- [ ] Verify cache strategy
- [ ] Test in private/incognito mode
- [ ] Clear all storage and retry

